tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-423-a-fixed-array-built-from-outside-a-group-is-told-once.hero:20:28: error[ffi_type]: `i64[2]` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (§4.19)
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-423-a-fixed-array-built-from-outside-a-group-is-told-once.hero:22:17: error[fixed_outside_a_group]: `i64[2]` is a C array member, so it stands only as a field of a `record` inside an `extern` group, whose layout a C compiler chose — here no group's record holds it (§4.19)
